I recently started playing Nethack again, and after several early
deaths,
I wondered "did I really win this game five times?". So I went diving
through Google Group's archives, and found that my YAFAP was dated
August 20th, 2001. I decided to try ascending on the 7th anniversary
of
that day.

So, last Sunday, I finally arrived on the Astral Plane, fought my way
to
all three altars and finally found the right one. I saved there, and
now
I can bring you this, my anniversary Valkyrie ascension.

A randomly generated throne gave me a genocide, which turned out to be
the
only opportunity for it in the whole game, and a wish, which went for
GDSM. That and the Sokoban amulet became the basis of my AK.

I *think* I started using Sunsword because I couldn't find any magic
lamps,
and the light from that was better than stumbling around mazes in the
dark.
I had it enchanted to +6 and it did a good job, but by the time I got
to
the Wizard it was down to +4 from disenchanters. I couldn't make a
*dent*
in him and had to use wands of death, of which there were only three
in
the whole game, and the rays kept missing.

Disenchanters were a huge pain in general, as were liches of all
kinds.
I found no scrolls of genocide and very little enchant foo, and only
one
wand of polymorph in the entire game, which turned all my spare
unicorn
horns into leashes and expensive cameras.

The lack of enchant weapon scrolls is why I never got around to using
Excalibur or Frost Brand, and ended up leaving them in my stash along
with Mjolnir. (I didn't even think of bringing them until I was
already
on the High Altar - stupid.)

Oddly enough, malignant auras were relatively harmless - my BoH got
uncursed once, and I arrived on the Astral plane with my onhand rings
being cursed. I forgot to even *try* to take off Conflict, but the
angels all killed each other without my help anyway.

In general, this was a very skin-of-my-teeth ascension, won more by
luck
and the resilience of the Valkyrie than any skill on my part.

